Data and model weights
----------------------

`data/` is not part of this repository (`docs/README.md` explains why: it is
1.1 GB of downloaded material this project did not author). The ECG it holds is

  Icentia11k Continuous ECG, via PhysioNet
  https://physionet.org/content/icentia11k-continuous-ecg/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
           International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

The classifier weights in `data/models/` were trained on that data and are
treated as a derivative of it: they carry the same CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 terms, not
MIT. A build that ships the weights is a non-commercial, share-alike build.

What that means in practice:

  * attribution is required -- keep this notice with any copy of the data or
    the weights;
  * commercial use of the data or the weights is not permitted, and the licence
    travels with anything derived from them;
  * the MIT licence on the code grants nothing about the data.

The bundled JavaScript dependencies (`app/package-lock.json`) and the Rust
crates (`app/src-tauri/Cargo.lock`) carry their own licences, mostly MIT and
Apache-2.0. The Python pipeline uses numpy, scipy, pandas, torch and Pillow,
each under its own licence at the version installed.

Third-party reference code
--------------------------

`app/src/lib/detect/gqrs.ts` is a port of the GQRS detrending and peak-detection
algorithm from WFDB (`wfdb.processing.gqrs_detect`), which is part of the
WFDB Python package, MIT licensed. `pipeline/*.py` uses `wfdb` to read the
PhysioNet annotation files. The algorithm is reproduced with its quirks intact
because the detector's measured performance depends on them; see
`docs/detector.md` and the header comment in `gqrs.ts`.
